  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with C-4-II through a shared pathway involving flavopiridol, which acts as a target of multiple enzymes. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets three distinct proteins—Cytochrome P450 2E1, Atypical kinase COQ8B, and Kappa-casein—each of which is targeted by flavopiridol. This indicates that flavopiridol may function as a common mediator in the downstream effects of Oblonganoside C, potentially modulating the activity of these enzymes and ultimately influencing C-4-II. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Oblonganoside C could exert its effects on C-4-II, possibly through the activation or inhibition of flavopiridol's target enzymes. The consistent involvement of flavopiridol as a bridge between Oblonganoside C and C-4-II supports a unified mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
